# Runtime settings for the deployed Cloud Functions.
#
#   cp functions/.env.example functions/.env
#
# THREE similarly-named things, easy to confuse:
#
#   functions/.env         shipped with a deploy, becomes runtime env vars.
#                          THIS is the one that affects the live functions.
#                          Gitignored, so CI writes it from repo variables --
#                          see "Write functions runtime env" in deploy.yml.
#                          A local copy only matters for a manual deploy.
#
#   functions/.env.local   read by the emulators and `functions:shell` only.
#                          Never deployed. Created automatically the first time
#                          the shell runs, which is why it may be the only one
#                          you have.
#
#   .env.local (repo root) the front-end's Firebase config, nothing to do with
#                          functions.
#
# Secrets do NOT go in any of these. API keys live in Secret Manager:
#   npx firebase-tools functions:secrets:set SENDGRID_API_KEY --project staging

# ---- Google Sheets sync -------------------------------------------------
# Spreadsheet ID from the sheet URL: /spreadsheets/d/<THIS>/edit
SHEET_ID=
SHEET_RANGE=Races!A1:E

# ---- Entry confirmation email -------------------------------------------
# Which provider to use: sendgrid or postmark. Leave blank to pick whichever
# credential is present in Secret Manager.
EMAIL_PROVIDER=

# The sending address. It does NOT need to be a real mailbox -- nothing has to
# receive at it -- but the domain must be authenticated with your provider, or
# every send is rejected.
ENTRY_EMAIL_FROM=no-reply@racewire.app
ENTRY_EMAIL_FROM_NAME=Racewire

# Where the "Review this entry" button in the organiser's notification points.
# Defaults to https://<project-id>.web.app, which is right until a custom domain
# is attached -- production serves racewire.app, so set it there.
APP_BASE_URL=

# FALLBACK reply-to only. Each event carries its own organiser email, set in
# the admin UI, and that is what confirmations for that event reply to. This is
# used when an event has none. Worth setting to an address somebody reads: a
# competitor who replies to a no-reply address otherwise gets silence, and entry
# questions are exactly the sort of thing they will reply with.
ENTRY_EMAIL_REPLY_TO=
